# Input
```vue
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->
<script lang="ts">
import type { Slot } from "vue";

export default {
  render() {
    this.$slots.default!(foo, bar);
    (this.$slots.default as Slot)(foo, bar);
    (this.$slots as Record<string, Slot>).default(foo, bar);

    const item = this.$slots.item!;
    item(foo, bar);
  },
};
</script>

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid-typescript.vue:7:31 lint/nursery/noVueMultipleSlotArgs ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! This slot is called with more than one argument.
  
    5 │ export default {
    6 │   render() {
  > 7 │     this.$slots.default!(foo, bar);
      │                               ^^^
    8 │     (this.$slots.default as Slot)(foo, bar);
    9 │     (this.$slots as Record<string, Slot>).default(foo, bar);
  
  i Slot content written in a template receives only the first argument, so the other arguments are lost.
  
  i Pass a single object that holds all the values, for example this.$slots.default({ item, index }).
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

